import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors","type":"adr","date":"2026-10","status":"accepted","status_note":"**Accepted (2026-10-15)** — the phase-1 measurement (carrier vs\\nfused on a real export at large T) passed: 1.82–2.33× at T=512,\\nwith extraction preferring the derived carrier.  The research bet\\n(proposer + constraint-synthesized guards) has its first\\nwitnesses: the game minted a conditional law and the synthesizer\\nnames its own gaps.  The open question has moved up a level —\\n**the form list and the mint target**, planned as 0024.\\n\\nThe architecture's fixed pieces are settled; what remains is the\\nadmission rate of the synthesized surface at the form level,\\nwhich only evidence settles."},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/adrs/0005-the-open-game.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/adrs/0005-the-open-game.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/adrs/0005-the-open-game.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0005-—-the-open-game-human-free-discovery-inside-anchored-anchors" tabindex="-1">ADR 0005 — The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0005-—-the-open-game-human-free-discovery-inside-anchored-anchors" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR 0005 — The open game: human-free discovery inside anchored anchors”">​</a></h1><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p><strong>The optimizer is an open game: every rule, object, vocabulary, runtime, and pricing inside it is machine-made data admitted by anchored machinery — and the only fixed pieces are the substrate, the correctness oracle, and the clock.</strong></p><p>Concretely:</p><ol><li><strong>Three anchors, nothing else.</strong> (a) <em>The substrate</em> — torch, GPU, the Triton compiler; the machine cannot mint the thing it runs on. (b) <em>The correctness oracle</em> — observational equivalence of outputs on real tensors plus certificate replay; a machine that could redefine equivalence voids every certificate, so the checker is machinery, not mintable data. (c) <em>The measured objective</em> — wall-clock time and memory on the substrate; a self-minted objective is a rigged race. Everything else — laws, guards, ops, carriers, runtimes, cost models, the proposal grammar — is inside the game.</li><li><strong>The VM picture is already the architecture.</strong> Ops are machine <em>descriptions</em> (<code>op</code> cells); handlers are machine <em>instantiations</em> (<code>handle</code> cells); the codegen tiers emit the runtimes (generated kernels are small minted VMs); carriers are state machines (<code>applyd</code> = <code>h ← a⊙h+x</code>). A cost model is a handler into flop/byte space — therefore mintable; only the <em>measured</em> referee stays anchored.</li><li><strong>The alphabet stays open by construction.</strong> New vocabulary enters two ways: composites (closed-form — <code>decay_vec</code> = <code>pow(γ, arange)</code>, retractible as a <em>declared</em> atom) and declared-op/generated-kernel atoms (open-form — semantics is the emitted code, verified observationally). The residual floor is whatever the substrate cannot express — universal computation is in reach; silicon is not.</li><li><strong>The learned prior guides a verified search — RL does not replace it.</strong> The verifier is perfect (exact + observational, no fuzzy reward), the cell store gives curriculum, and imitation on claiming traces already warm-starts the policy. What RL does not fix: candidate density (~10⁹ law shapes, most invalid), cold start, and credit assignment across pattern + guard + derive. Guard synthesis is constraint-solving — conds are already data — not a policy problem. Quality-diversity beats raw RL for frontier coverage.</li><li><strong>The four dimensions hold at the meta level too.</strong> A synthesized law/guard/runtime is a <em>search</em> artifact that must pass the same semantics gate a shipped <code>R(...)</code> passes — numeric oracle → typed-pay gate → certificate replay → adversarial sweep of the guard&#39;s false region. Admission is never a vote the machine casts for itself.</li></ol><h2 id="why" tabindex="-1">Why <a class="header-anchor" href="#why" aria-label="Permalink to “Why”">​</a></h2><p>ADR 0004 opened the move set: constructed objects — folds, bridges, carriers — are admissible <em>data</em>, not pre-approved Python. Since then the machinery closed a demonstrable loop: on <code>torch.export(ChunkedRetention)</code>, equality saturation under a guarded law set produces <code>decay</code>, <code>decay_vec</code>, and folded <code>applyd</code>/<code>aff_diag</code> carriers unaided; the scan tier lowers those carriers into real <code>triton.jit</code> kernels verified to ~1e-16 on CUDA; minted composites land in the cell store as <code>op</code> cells the registry walks uniformly.</p><h2 id="not-doing" tabindex="-1">Not doing <a class="header-anchor" href="#not-doing" aria-label="Permalink to “Not doing”">​</a></h2><ul><li>none recorded — legacy record; the design doc lists what was deferred.</li></ul><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li>**The repository shrinks to machinery + the declaration</li><li><strong>The measured win is the phase-1 gate.</strong> Nothing is</li><li><strong>Guard synthesis is the research bet.</strong> If proposer +</li><li><strong>Honest scars carried forward</strong> (updated 2026-10-15; closed</li><li><strong>What this is not.</strong> Not RL solving search; not an LLM</li></ul><h2 id="enforcement" tabindex="-1">Enforcement <a class="header-anchor" href="#enforcement" aria-label="Permalink to “Enforcement”">​</a></h2><ul><li>Code and tests are named in the design doc.</li></ul><h2 id="design" tabindex="-1">Design <a class="header-anchor" href="#design" aria-label="Permalink to “Design”">​</a></h2><p>The full record (context, tables, phases, trade-offs): <a href="./../design/0005-the-open-game.html"><code>design/0005-the-open-game.md</code></a>.</p>`,15)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};